# Executive and Technical Security Assessment

## 1. Executive Summary

This assessment provides an executive and technical review of the authorized demo security scope. The review focused on identifying security weaknesses, assessing associated risks, and recommending practical remediation measures.

Five security findings were consolidated and assessed using a consistent likelihood and impact methodology. Four findings were rated High risk and one was rated Medium risk.

The most significant areas requiring attention are authentication security, access control, security logging and monitoring, and backup/recovery preparedness.

Overall, the assessment indicates that the demo environment would benefit from stronger preventive controls, improved monitoring, and documented recovery procedures.

## 2. Assessment Scope

The assessment was conducted against the authorized demo scope only.

The review considered:

- Asset identification and inventory
- Authentication and password practices
- Access control and user permissions
- Services and exposed functionality
- Security logging and monitoring
- Backup and recovery preparedness
- Remediation priorities
- Incident-response preparedness

No unauthorized systems were tested.

